{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Runtime budgets (#6). calibration holds the traces the limits are set from: pnpm test:trace measures, and tests/trace/calibrate.mjs writes each entry from its report. Each entry names what it traced by content: the base commit the app sat on and the git tree ids of its apps and packages.",
  "notes": {
    "unmapped": "(unmapped) is chunk bytes no source mapping covers: module wrappers, the bundler glue, and line breaks. It belongs to no package; slice 3 decides whether it counts as platform JS.",
    "dataUrls": "Playwright reports no request for a data: URL, so the complete fixture, whose images are all data URLs, shows 0 image requests and 0 image bytes: those bytes are in the document. Image budgets need a fixture with image files.",
    "analyzeBytes": "A PORTFOLIO_ANALYZE=1 build's chunks end in sourceMappingURL comments, so their bytes run a little over the default build's: take byte limits from a default build, and attribution from an analyze build.",
    "conditions": "Each viewport's conditions are what its case ran under. webgl says whether getContext('webgl') and getContext('webgl2') gave a context; false is null, as in the headless shell with no GPU, so a variant that draws with WebGL draws nothing there and its frame, canvas, and long-task numbers understate it. dpr is window.devicePixelRatio, and loadAverage the machine's 1-minute load as the case ended."
  },
  "forbidden": {
    "description": "Source modules no owner or read-only public page may load (#6, Slice 2). pnpm test:trace matches every module of every chunk a public page downloads, or its HTML and RSC payload name, against these globs, through source maps (tests/harness/trace/purity.mjs). Each glob is a path under apps/ or packages/, relative to the repository root, and has to match a file there: one that matches nothing fails the trace and pnpm test. Units other than the one a page renders are checked from ASSET_MANIFEST, so they aren't listed here. #8, #9, and #20 add their Studio, demo, and research paths as they land, and slice 6 adds apps/web/src/lib/studio/**.",
    "modules": [
      {
        "glob": "apps/web/src/app/(studio)/**",
        "rationale": "Studio's pages, layout, and styles (#2, #8): the owner's surface, never a visitor's."
      },
      {
        "glob": "apps/web/src/app/(preview)/**",
        "rationale": "The preview's frame document and grant routes (#7): owner-only, loaded inside Studio."
      },
      {
        "glob": "apps/web/src/preview/**",
        "rationale": "The preview's agent and status document (#7): a frame's code, never a public page's."
      },
      {
        "glob": "apps/web/src/app/host-chrome.css",
        "rationale": "The host chrome's styles (#7), which Studio and the preview document link: a public page's CSS is experience-base.css and its units' alone."
      },
      {
        "glob": "apps/web/src/server/demo/**",
        "rationale": "The demo's code (#9), the read-only reference's opener among it: the composition root loads it under demo alone, so no owner or read-only page names or loads it."
      }
    ]
  },
  "budgets": {
    "description": "The ceilings each unit's declared budgets are held to (#6, items 3 and 4): one row per variant tier and one per appearance pack axis, in the six kinds a manifest declares. A kind a unit leaves out is its ceiling, and a declared one over its ceiling fails. pnpm check:budgets measures each registered unit from the build output, ASSET_MANIFEST, and the trace report, and writes one failure record per breach. A ceiling changes only in a reviewed edit to this file, with its basis.",
    "kinds": {
      "js": "gzip bytes of the unit's own JavaScript a route downloads as it loads, by source-map attribution, its enhancement chunks left out",
      "css": "gzip bytes of the unit's compiled stylesheet, the kit's shared renderers' layout included for a variant",
      "image": "bytes of the image files the unit ships",
      "font": "bytes of the font files the unit ships",
      "animation": "continuous work on an active, idle page, as the trace probes count it: frame loops, recurring timers, and running infinite animations",
      "enhancement": "gzip bytes of every chunk one of the unit's enhancements loads, the one holding its entry and each other its async chunk group loads with it: its own code, and the kit's and every library's"
    },
    "headroom": "Kind by kind. JS: light 30,720, under the 43,879 of variant code v1 Editorial's page carried over the fallback route's, and medium and heavy 92,160, twice that; slice 2's largest variant, fixture-variant-medium, measured 926. CSS: light 10,240, two thirds of v1's one 14,494 B file of every variant's CSS, and medium and heavy 15,360, above that whole file; slice 2's largest, fixture-variant-medium, compiled 1,184. Image and font: v1 has no measurement of either, since its images were data URLs and its fonts came from Google, so they start at #6's original 102,400, with 204,800 and 409,600 for medium and heavy images. Animation: light 0, as v1 Editorial ran nothing while idle; medium 3, one over the 2 CI measured for fixture-variant-medium, its shader's frame loop and one infinite CSS animation; heavy 4. Heavy shares medium's JS, CSS, and font ceilings because slice 1 traced no heavy composition to set its own from. Pack rows rest on the same measurements, per the basis below.",
    "tiers": {
      "light": {
        "js": 30720,
        "css": 10240,
        "image": 102400,
        "font": 102400,
        "animation": 0,
        "enhancement": 15360
      },
      "medium": {
        "js": 92160,
        "css": 15360,
        "image": 204800,
        "font": 102400,
        "animation": 3,
        "enhancement": 92160
      },
      "heavy": {
        "js": 92160,
        "css": 15360,
        "image": 409600,
        "font": 102400,
        "animation": 4,
        "enhancement": 307200
      }
    },
    "packs": {
      "color-scheme": {
        "js": 0,
        "css": 3072,
        "image": 0,
        "font": 0,
        "animation": 0,
        "enhancement": 0
      },
      "typography": {
        "js": 0,
        "css": 3072,
        "image": 0,
        "font": 102400,
        "animation": 0,
        "enhancement": 0
      },
      "design-language": {
        "js": 15360,
        "css": 12288,
        "image": 51200,
        "font": 0,
        "animation": 1,
        "enhancement": 15360
      }
    },
    "basis": {
      "js": {
        "restsOn": [
          "/calibration/baseline-editorial/viewports/1440x900/js/gzipBytes",
          "/calibration/fallback-route/viewports/1440x900/js/gzipBytes"
        ],
        "why": "v1 Editorial's page carried every v1 variant's code over the platform, about 44 KB more than the fallback route's. A light variant gets 30 KB, most of that for one variant; medium and heavy get 90 KB, twice all of it. Slice 2's trace at 055f1f4 measured 125 B of fixture-variant-light and 926 B of fixture-variant-medium."
      },
      "css": {
        "restsOn": ["/calibration/baseline-editorial/viewports/1440x900/css/gzipBytes"],
        "why": "v1 shipped every variant's CSS in one 14.5 KB file. Medium and heavy get about that whole file, 15 KB, and light two thirds of it, 10 KB. Slice 2 compiled 924 B for the fallback composition, 933 B for fixture-variant-light, and 1184 B for fixture-variant-medium. Packs: v1's file again, against slice 2's 1979 B for warm-parchment, 739 B for platform-neutral, and 648 B for humanist-ui, so a scheme and a typography profile get 3 KB each and a design language, which carries layout, 12 KB."
      },
      "image": {
        "restsOn": [
          "/calibration/baseline-editorial/viewports/1440x900/images/bytes",
          "/notes/dataUrls"
        ],
        "why": "Slice 1 measured no image bytes: the complete fixture's images are data URLs. The tiers keep #6's original 100, 200, and 400 KB until a fixture with image files is traced; slice 2's medium still is 302 B. A design language may ship 50 KB of textures."
      },
      "font": {
        "restsOn": [
          "/calibration/baseline-editorial/viewports/1440x900/fonts/bytes",
          "/calibration/baseline-editorial/viewports/1440x900/thirdParty/count"
        ],
        "why": "v1 fetched its fonts from Google, which the trace blocks, so it measured 0 font bytes and 3 third-party requests. Self-hosted fonts get #6's original 100 KB, for a variant and for a typography profile alike; schemes and design languages ship none."
      },
      "animation": {
        "restsOn": [
          "/calibration/baseline-editorial/viewports/1440x900/counters/frameLoops",
          "/calibration/baseline-editorial/viewports/1440x900/counters/recurringTimers",
          "/calibration/baseline-editorial/viewports/1440x900/counters/infiniteAnimations"
        ],
        "why": "v1 Editorial, a light variant, ran no loop, timer, or infinite animation while idle, so light gets 0. fixture-variant-medium runs 1 infinite animation, plus its shader's frame loop where WebGL2 draws, 2 in CI, so medium gets 3, one to spare, and heavy 4. A design language gets 1, for an ambient effect."
      },
      "enhancement": {
        "restsOn": ["/calibration/baseline-editorial/viewports/1440x900/js/gzipBytes"],
        "why": "v1 had no enhancements, so its whole page's JavaScript is the scale. Light gets 15 KB, medium 90 KB, and heavy #6's original one enhancement chunk of up to 300 KB, under v1's 286 KB page plus room. A design language's behavior gets 15 KB."
      }
    }
  },
